nformation as usual. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Ahead, "Daily Show" host, Trevor Noah will join us right here in studio with an exclusive announcement. You do not want to miss this, so don`t you go anywhere.\par \par \uc2 But first it is 8:08, time to check your local weather.\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Coming up, Anthony Mason speaks with two-time Rock and Roll Hall of Famer, Graham Nash about his new book of photography.\par \par \uc2 (Begin VT)\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: What is that pleasure you get when you take a great photograph?\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM NASH (Rock and roll hall of Famer): Something I found that nobody else found.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: So you`re collecting -- you`re collecting feelings?\par \par \uc2 GRAHAM NASH: Yes. Namely, I`m doing the same with my music.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Oh man, speaking of his music, that is one of my favorite Crosby Stills and Nash songs, Southern Cross playing there. So, why Nash tries to be invisible when he holds a camera and some of his favorite photos of his former bandmates, David Crosby, Stephen Stills, and \uc2 Neil Young\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: It`s like better than, our house is a very, very ...\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It is a good one, Gayle. For "Sweet Judy Brown Eyes." "Sweet Judy Brown Eyes."\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Life used to be so hard.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Love that. Love everything that they do. This is \uc2 CBS\uc2  MORNINGS.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Go Gayle.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 (Video of Woodstock: 3 Days of Peace and Music.)\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Yes, that`s Crosby Stills and Nash performing at Woodstock in 1969. It was only their second gig together. The group`s rise to fame with the addition of \uc2 Neil Young\uc2  and all of the subsequent turbulence 