big is the bump-up in pay?\par \par \uc2 JOE (Army Veteran: Twenty-five percent.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: As soon as Joe, an army veteran, got to the ATF`s human resources department in 2016, he said he noticed personnel problems.\par \par \uc2 JOE: They would bring every agent that wanted to be promoted to th the headquarters and spend time there doing a whole lot of jobs.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: Desk jobs?\par \par \uc2 JOE: Desk jobs, a variety of jobs, to which they weren`t even minimally qualified.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: And Joe told us there was another issue.\par \par \uc2 Even though some ATF personnel were doing administrative jobs, Joe told us they were paid a bonus known as law enforcement availability pay or LEAP for short.\par \par \uc2 JOE: People who were receiving it in positions where they weren`t authorized.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: Government regulations stipulate the extra pay is reserved for criminal investigators who are on call and expected to work unscheduled additional hours.\par \par \uc2 How much money are we talking about for a individual employee?\par \par \uc2 JOE: If you were making $100,000 and you got LEAP, you would get $125,000.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: Joe doesn`t know how long it`s been going on or how much money has been wasted, but colleagues told him --\par \par \uc2 JOE: That was the ATF way.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: What do you mean the ATF way?\par \par \uc2 JOE: This is what they have done for 30-plus-years to what I was told.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: After telling a senior ATF official in 2018 what he found, Joe got this email from his supervisor sayings his bosses were upset. Joe`s performance reviews went from "fully successful" before going to management to "minimally successful" after.\par \par \uc2 What did you take away as the message?\par \par \uc2 JOE: Don`t look over there. Just because you see somebody stealing money out the ATM, you don`t have to say anything.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: In June last year, a federal lawyer told Joe the \uc2 Office of Special Counsel\uc2  found la substantial likelihood of wrongdoing. Since, the government`s HR office suspended the ATF`s authority to create certain jobs for no less than six months.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR \uc2 CHUCK GRASSLEY\uc2  (R-Iowa): This seems to be a waste of taxpayers` money.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: Senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2  is the top Republican on the Senate committee with direct oversight of the ATF. While four agencies are investigating Joe`s case over a three-year period, none of it reached Grassley`s office.\par \par \uc2 Should someone have told your committee?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR \uc2 CHUCK GRASSLEY\uc2 : You are absolutely right. It boils down to the fact that agencies don`t like to be embarrassed by these revelations that come from whistleblowers.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: Because of the \uc2 CBS\uc2  report, Grassley`s investigators sent these letters to the ATF, the Justice Department and the federal government`s HR agency, demanding records and answers.\par \par \uc2 Will you ask your investigators to find out if it`s happening at other agencies?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR \uc2 CHUCK GRASSLEY\uc2 : Well, my suspicion is it probably is. We are going to find out how widespread it is.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: Four months ago, Joe lost his job. His supervisor said he was inconsistent following instructions and argumentative among other issues.\par \par \uc2 Are you a difficult employee?\par \par \uc2 JOE: If what you`re asking me to do is illegal, unethical, immoral, yes, I`m going to be difficult because I`m not going to do it.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE HERRIDGE: An email from the \uc2 Office of Special Counsel\uc2  reviewed by CBS News says a final report into Joe`s claims delayed, citing broad implications for the ATF. Four government agencies declined to answer our questions, and n