d): Honestly, it feels, it feels like two seconds and 40 minutes at the same time. I just kind of heard yelling over everything. I don`t know, I kind of just do that when everything is, like, really loud, I kind of just tune what people are saying out.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI BATTISTE: Video also shows Cox being questioned. He died of natural causes in December of 2019 before any charges were filed against him.\par \par \uc2 Lori Vallow and her new husband, Chad Daybell, have pleaded not guilty to killing J.J. and Tylee who were reported missing in the fall of 2019. Their remains found in Daybell`s backyard the following summer.\par \par \uc2 The investigation expanded to include the deaths of Chad`s first wife, Tammy, Lori`s ex-husband, Charles Vallow, and her brother, Alex Cox, who killed Vallow, claiming self-defense.\par \par \uc2 MAN: Just tell people what`s happening.\par \par \uc2 NIKKI BATTISTE: After his wife`s death, Chad and Lori Daybell married and later moved to Hawaii alone.\par \par \uc2 The couple is also accused of profiting from the deaths. Court documents reveal Chad took out a large life insurance policy on Tammy, and Lori continued to collect her children`s Social Security survivor benefits after their deaths.\par \par \uc2 Lori Vallow has later charged in Charles Vallow`s murder, accused of conspiring with Cox in the killing.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Chad Daybell has pleaded not guilty and is facing the penalty for the murder of the children.\par \par \uc2 Lori Vallow`s case is on hold. She remains in custody after being deemed not competent to stand trial.\par \par \uc2 For \uc2 CBS\uc2  MORNINGS, I`m Nikki Battiste in New York.\par \par \uc2 (End VT)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: I don`t even know what you say after that, it`s just so bizarre and so tragic. It`s very tough to see the little girl talking, though, two months before she was killed and then found on the property of the man that her mother married. It`s --\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Yeah, you oftentimes think you couldn`t script this in a movie and then think about the ripple effect of people actually being killed.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: And then you think, Nate, in a movie, nobody would believe it because it`s this and this and this and this.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: Listen, coming up, Vlad Duthiers, he has the stories that you will be talking about.\par \par \uc2 But, first, it`s 7:42. Time to check your local weather.\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Vlad Duthiers picking his intro music today.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: I would love to say this is about me, but it is not about me actually.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Wait, Vlad, wait. You would love to say that`s about you? Simply the best?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Simply the best trivial pursuit player or simply the best movie nerd or Jedi, but it is not about me.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Okay, who`s it about?\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: It`s about Tina Turner.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: She is simply the best.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Right?\par \par \uc2 Tina is simply the best, and she`s rolling in the dough after signing a mega music deal. Check this out.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Are you cracking yourself up?\par \par \uc2 Everybody has got to do the move, the Tina move, right? Here`s why. Tia Turner sold the rights to six decades of her music, including her hits, "Proud Mary", "What`s Love Got To Do With It", and "The Best" to the music publishing company BMG. The deal not only covers her artist and writers` share of recordings, but also the management of Turner`s name and image.\par \par \uc2 Insider estimates the deal is worth more than $50 million. That`s kind of low to me. Tina deserves more.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 VLADIMIR DUTHIERS: Turner said the move is part of an effort to preserve her legacy. She is set to be inducted into the Rock `N` Roll Hall of Fame for a second t