c2 All right, Vlad, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, Anthony Mason visits two-time Grammy winner and hit songwriter Natalie Hemby in Nashville. He`s in our green room with more. There`s Anthony.\par \par \uc2 GAYE KING: Hey.\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (LOCAL WEATHER)\par \par \uc2 (ANNOUNCEMENTS)\par \par \uc2 *************************************************************************** *********** (08:00am ET)\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Welcome back to \uc2 CBS\uc2  MORNINGS. I`m Gayle King.\par \par \uc2 Coming up in this hour, Grammy winner Natalie Hemby is finally stepping into the spotlight after writing some massive hits.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: I`m Tony Dokoupil.\par \par \uc2 Can humans and sharks ever get along?\par \par \uc2 We`ll tell you what`s behind a new effort to track the predators off the California coast.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: I`m Nate Burleson and improvising rhymes and complicated times.\par \par \uc2 See what I did there?\par \par \uc2 We`re talking to Christopher Jackson of the Tony-winning Freestyle Love Supreme.\par \par \uc2 GAYLE KING: Nicely done.\par \par \uc2 But first, here`s today`s eye-opener at 8:00.\par \par \uc2 A compromise deal may be close in Washington on raising the debt ceiling. Some Democrats say it`s just kicking the can down the road.\par \par \uc2 MAN: I`m sure you`ve done it. I do it every once in a while. You hit the snooze button to delay the inevitable before you get out of bed. Well, look, that`s what Congress is doing right now.\par \par \uc2 TONY DOKOUPIL: Four people are wounded in a shooting at a school in Arlington, Texas. Police say it started with a fight.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN: Today could have ended so much differently. I`m very thankful to have my daughter with me.\par \par \uc2 NATE BURLESON: For the first time in history, the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  endorses a malaria vaccine. Scientists believe it could save tens of thousands of