Y MASON: Hemby, who grew up around Nashville, near the mother church of country music, got some advice from another musician that day.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE HEMBY: She said, don`t be nervous, just look at the stained glass windows.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: These right here?\par \par \uc2 NATALIE HEMBY: Yes. She said just imagine heaven`s light shining down on you.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Did it work?\par \par \uc2 NATALIE HEMBY: It did work. It`s worked every time.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: And for a moment, it looked like the light would shine.\par \par \uc2 You almost got a recording deal at 20.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE HEMBY: Yes. I was around 19 or 20.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: But it fell through.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE HEMBY: And I was devastated at the time. Then I started getting to a point where I was like, I just want to do music. I really don`t care what that looks like anymore.\par \par \uc2 (MUSIC PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: So she started writing songs.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE HEMBY: I always say I wrote my way into this business. And I really did.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Hemby`s breakthrough came more than a decade later, when she teamed up with Miranda Lambert.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE HEMBY: We hit it off. It went so well, we wrote four songs in one day and then another day we wrote another four songs. Miranda has been such a blessing to me, this girl from Texas. I`ve had over 30 cuts with her.\par \par \uc2 (MUSIC PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: "White Liar" in 2010 would be the first number one for both of them. But Hemby was surprised at her own reaction.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE HEMBY: I felt sad inside.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: For having a number one song?\par \par \uc2 NATALIE HEMBY: Yes.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: She asked a songwriting friend what was wrong with her.\par \par \uc2 NATALIE HEMBY: And he was like, you know, it`s because you think you can`t do it again. It`s over.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY MASON: Is 