dships, business relationships, and I just think that just don`t play it small. You know, if you have to shrink yourself to be around who you`re - who you`re being around, I think, you know, you might need to find new people.\par \par \uc2 KING: How did you come up with the title Star Crossed?\par \par \uc2 MUSGRAVES: It just popped in my mind. Like, I thought about all these great tragedies over time, right? You know, these, these love stories, these - something that we can all relate to. And I thought about Romeo and Juliet. And then I thought about the word star crossed and what it means.\par \par \uc2 KING: And you did a movie to go along with it, too. Now, I thought the movie was fun.\par \par \uc2 MUSGRAVES: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 KING: Also very deep.\par \par \uc2 MUSGRAVES: There`s so - so many layers of real emotion, real experiences, everything that you see there was done for a reason. Everything is very intentional. It`s a hyper real kind of fantastical way of portraying this journey that I`ve been on through healing. And along the way. I mean, there`s like, there`s look served, you know, there`s, it was really fun. It was, it was mostly so fun.\par \par \uc2 KING: You know, I remember, were we in South Africa, when you were performing Golden Hour?\par \par \uc2 MUSGRAVES: Yes.\par \par \uc2 KING: You were so giddy and so happy. And that`s where you were at that time in your life. When you look back on it now, does it - does that album feel tainted to you? Or no, not really.\par \par \uc2 MUSGRAVES: For a while I was nervous. Because, you know, I know that a lot of people love those songs. And when they come see you play, you want to give people what they want to hear. And for a while, I was like, Man, it`s going to be so painful for me having to go back there. But ultimately, I`m in a different place in my life now. I can say that I`m happy. And I`m kind of looking in on that other chapter from another side.\par \par \uc2 And I really don`t think that